    <bpmn:process id="W_W1898" name="W1898. Contractor Advisory Board &amp; Feedback Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual advisory board formation; quarterly meetings
Frequency: Quarterly meetings
Volume: ~15–20 advisory board members (top contractors across regions and trade types)
Owner: VP Store Operations
Participants: VP Store Operations, Category Manager, VP Merchandising, Advisory Board Members
Source: workflow W1898 — Contractor Advisory Board &amp; Feedback Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1898_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1898_Lane1" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1898_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1898_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1898_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1898_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1898_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1898_Start3" name="Annual advisory board formation; quarterly meetings">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1898_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1898_Task4" name="Annual: VP Store Operations selects advisory board members: (a) top 5…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual: VP Store Operations selects advisory board members: (a) top 5 contractors by revenue from each region (Mindanao, Visayas, Luzon, NCR), (b) mix of trade types: general construction, electrical, plumbing, interior design, (c) 2-year rotating membership with 50% retention for continuity, (d) advisory board benefits: exclusive pricing tier, quarterly dinner meetings, direct channel to VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1898_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1898_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1898_Task5" name="Quarterly: VP Store Operations hosts advisory board meeting: (a) present…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly: VP Store Operations hosts advisory board meeting: (a) present BuildRight initiatives: new products, service improvements, technology roadmap, (b) solicit feedback: what products are missing? What service improvements would help their business? What are their biggest pain points?, (c) discuss industry trends: construction market outlook, regulatory changes, labor availability, (d) review action items from previous meeting: what has BuildRight implemented based on board recommendations?
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Half-day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1898_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1898_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1898_Task6" name="Post-meeting: (a) VP Store Operations distributes meeting summary and action…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Post-meeting: (a) VP Store Operations distributes meeting summary and action items to relevant departments (Merchandising, Supply Chain, IT, Store Operations), (b) track action item completion for next meeting, (c) incorporate board feedback into planning: product assortment, service design, pricing strategy
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1898_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1898_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1898_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
